\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{A finite Borel–Pompeiu formula}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{The counting operator on the cubical torus is self-adjoint. For
any set of cubes, the failure of that adjoint identity on the set
equals the counting difference on the complement.}

\p{Over an ordered field the counting form splits off the harmonic
cochains. The inverse of the operator on the complement satisfies
#{\extD E=I-H}. The pairing of a cochain against a test cochain on a
set of cubes is the source term, the meeting pairing, and the
harmonic term. On the whole torus this is #{F=E(\extD F)+HF}.}

\p{The identity holds in every dimension. On a cycle, an arc
reduces to a telescoping sum and to the terminating
forward-difference formula.}

\transclude{fdip-00P3}
